    {
      "type": "examAlert",
      "items": [
        "Wilhelm Wundt is regarded as the Father of Experimental Psychology.",
        "Classical Conditioning (Pavlov) focuses on Stimulus-Response (S-R), whereas Operant Conditioning (Skinner) focuses on Response-Stimulus (R-S) reinforcement.",
        "Lewis Terman introduced the formula for Intelligence Quotient: IQ = (Mental Age / Chronological Age) × 100.",
        "The exact sequence of Maslow's Hierarchy is: Physiological → Safety → Love/Belonging → Esteem → Self-Actualization."
      ],
      "id": "v2q2elj"
    },
